    "summary": "Interprets the clean-copy repeat receipt e7a4c652bb2b4273972d661adccd41e9 of b5bd70f5750b4b45af3e925bd1748aaf-experiment and rewrites the phantom-configuration account (6491640ed49a4c7b8f5150438d350e36-question-0) around what that receipt shows. The shrink direction reproduced field for field: latest index ahead of the stored log, removal reported as failed, re-election under the single-server phantom configuration, commit_index=4 with the peer at 2, then restart re-leading with the peer catching up to 5. With the third and fourth receipts covering the swapped member assignment, the unsupported commit now rests on four receipts, so the reproducibility and restart statements move from one run to two and the old each-once/no-repetition limitation is replaced. The repeat also refuted a load-bearing premise in the previous explanation: the record claimed a grown phantom quorum still contains a majority of committed voters, but a grown phantom configuration {A,B,C} admits the quorum {A,C}, which omits B entirely; the absence of an unsupported commit in the grow direction came from the harness adding an unreachable third voter, so {A,B} was the only attainable quorum. The grow direction also behaved differently this time (no re-election inside the ten-second window, apply failed, both stores ending at index 3), so its earlier no-unsupported-commit reading is now stated as an absent commit rather than a quorum-held one, and a limitation records that the {A,C}-style quorum remains untested. Knowledge entries 6491640ed49a4c7b8f5150438d350e36-knowledge-0 and -1 carry the new receipt's executions for unchanged behaviour statements. Conclusion stays violated with the defect asserted; the submission validates with zero schema errors and requests no further execution."
